{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body","id":1349873,"title":"What happens to an undone Arcadian Sidhe's body?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-20T09:39:55-08:00","id":1349873,"title":"What happens to an undone Arcadian Sidhe's body?","content":"Exactly what it says on the subject line. A commoner or Autumn Sidhe is down for the count, at least until they're reborn, but as I understand it there's nothing left of the original person inside for the Sidhe.<br /> <br /> Google hasn't helped me out here. Does the body die? Go catatonic? Operate off rote repetitions and rhythms until something unexpected happens?<br /> <br /> This isn't important per se to the game I'm in, but the question popped up and I'm wondering what, if anything, is the canon answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T10:18:28-08:00","id":1349880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body#post1349873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly what it says on the subject line. A commoner or Autumn Sidhe is down for the count, at least until they're reborn, but as I understand it there's nothing left of the original person inside for the Sidhe.</div> </div> </div> </div>This not the case. I mean his soul might be gone but what mortal memories were made remain. You get a mix of people with lost time(ala the rip van winkle in the core) and people who just seem to have more mundane fadings. Either way it doesn't look any different from other Fae as the soul is a sleep in the body of a mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T12:15:27-08:00","id":1349901,"title":"","content":"Aye, they may still be able to function but they are essentially going to be operating entirely off of memory as the person's soul is gone (to the best of our canon knowledge) and the fae soul will be dormant while undone.<br /> <br /> I could see that being interpreted as anything from going catatonic to being cold and soulless to just performing off of rote actions and/or instincts depending on the needs of the character as well as the table/game/chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T04:34:25-08:00","id":1349999,"title":"","content":"Once upon a time I knew a guy named Dare. He was a local musician who seemed permanently young. He was handsome, loved by the ladies, an excellent musician. The guy drank most nights and never seemed to sleep and was slim and fit despite a diet of beer, grease and sugar. He also was a wonderful person, taking care of house bound elders on his own dime.<br /> <br /> Then, over the course of a few months, he aged and died. Like a switch was flipped. It was awful. He just fell apart.<br /> <br /> This is how I think of Sidhe and other fae being undone. The light that shown so bright gets snuffed, and they fade away. And the world is colder and darker from their passing. Though most times the loss of a fae spirit will not kill the mortal shell, but the character will become a sadder, less vibrant person. Such a person might seem to age more quickly, fall into depression, alcoholism, or just get lost in the day to day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 11-21-2019, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T10:27:53-08:00","id":1350046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body?p=1349901#post1349901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aye, they may still be able to function but they are essentially going to be operating entirely off of memory as the person's soul is gone (to the best of our canon knowledge) and the fae soul will be dormant while undone.<br /> <br /> I could see that being interpreted as anything from going catatonic to being cold and soulless to just performing off of rote actions and/or instincts depending on the needs of the character as well as the table/game/chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They aren't soulless their fairy nature is asleep until the death of the body. THat's what Undone are. Arcadian Fairies are no different than Autumn fairies who are undone. They have still picked up some level of mortal memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T15:42:15-08:00","id":1350141,"title":"","content":"Arcadians are distinct from their Autumn counterparts. Arcadians don't follow the Changeling Way and they don't create the same sort of arguably symbiotic relationship with their mortal hosts, including their souls, that Autumn fae do.<br /> <br /> Arcadians are body snatchers. They dislodge the human soul and fully take over. They don't reincarnate and according to the sources we have their mortal souls are trapped somewhere far away after the Arcadians take over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T16:21:38-08:00","id":1350146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body?p=1350141#post1350141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcadians are distinct from their Autumn counterparts. Arcadians don't follow the Changeling Way and they don't create the same sort of arguably symbiotic relationship with their mortal hosts, including their souls, that Autumn fae do.<br /> <br /> Arcadians are body snatchers. They dislodge the human soul and fully take over. They don't reincarnate and according to the sources we have their mortal souls are trapped somewhere far away after the Arcadians take over.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. They would be grey, listless persons. Perhaps even prime examples of persons with the 5pt &quot;Psychic Vampire&quot; flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T17:49:31-08:00","id":1350155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body?p=1350141#post1350141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcadians are distinct from their Autumn counterparts. Arcadians don't follow the Changeling Way and they don't create the same sort of arguably symbiotic relationship with their mortal hosts, including their souls, that Autumn fae do<br /> <br /> Arcadians are body snatchers. They dislodge the human soul and fully take over. They don't reincarnate and according to the sources we have their mortal souls are trapped somewhere far away after the Arcadians take over.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they don't look any different when their souls are asleep. I can go through the books Arcadian Sidhe aren't treated as anything special when they aren't awake, they have normal down times if chimerically killled. They have normal undoings. You'd think if a whole Kith had special mechanics for Chimerical death and Undoing it would come up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T11:37:21-08:00","id":1350273,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying they aren't undone and aren't chimerically killed, I'm just gonna say that I don't personally think you can treat their mortal selves while in such states the same way that you can treat any other mortal, because they are missing an integral element of there being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T16:42:45-08:00","id":1350342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body?p=1350273#post1350273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying they aren't undone and aren't chimerically killed, I'm just gonna say that I don't personally think you can treat their mortal selves while in such states the same way that you can treat any other mortal, because they are missing an integral element of there being.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I am saying there's no basis that having a sleeping soul does anything. IF we include OTHER gamelines... the vast majority of normal people have sleeping souls. They are not missing anything. They are asleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T16:34:11-08:00","id":1350539,"title":"","content":"I'm not referring to the human soul being asleep, the fae soul is dormant during such periods. In the Arcadians, the human soul is not asleep. It is gone. It has been expelled to allow the Arcadian Fae soul to entrench.<br /> <br /> This is the difference between Arcadian hosts and changeling hosts that I've been trying to illustrate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T18:56:49-08:00","id":1350749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body?p=1350539#post1350539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not referring to the human soul being asleep, the fae soul is dormant during such periods. In the Arcadians, the human soul is not asleep. It is gone. It has been expelled to allow the Arcadian Fae soul to entrench.<br /> <br /> This is the difference between Arcadian hosts and changeling hosts that I've been trying to illustrate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a difference. And for the fairies and wizards of the world it matters. It matters that there's someone who's basically getting the short end of C:TL thanks to the Arcadian Fae. But it doesn't matter to common folk. IT doesn't leave behind something unique or special. That wouldn't be Banal. Comas, sudden deaths, these are EXCITING. IT doesn't leave behind an artist, that's for sure. They aren't going to be developing new theories or innovating... it just leaves behind another banal cog.<br /> <br /> IF you want to engage in the &quot;you're a horrible body snatcher&quot; plot that's when the Arcadian is actually active.. maybe you bring the Tithed or a Kermet into play, maybe you have someone freak out about how they've completely changed like in Ascendency of a Bookworm... but once they have fallen to Banality... that's the end of interesting moments.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T10:32:31-08:00","id":1350852,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, maybe it's because I don't get the references, except for the CtL one, but I'm not totally sure what you're getting at here. Could you please clarify?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T16:20:17-08:00","id":1350922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body?p=1350852#post1350852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, maybe it's because I don't get the references, except for the CtL one, but I'm not totally sure what you're getting at here. Could you please clarify?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So I'm still eyeing the thread and taking this in, but I think the point is that the mortal soul who gets evicted for an Arcadian fae has a parallel to the changelings in Lost, who are humans stolen away to faerie lands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T16:34:58-08:00","id":1350926,"title":"","content":"Sure, I get that much, I'm just not sure how that relates to Lian's final point, nor am I entirely certain what that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T05:19:33-08:00","id":1351016,"title":"","content":"If I understand correctly, Lian's argument here is that there are differences, sure. But once a Changeling is undone they don't get anything &quot;interesting.&quot; Drama, adventure, tragedy, tension, these are all things that happen for people who still have a spark in them. <br /> <br /> An undone Changeling doesn't get to live in interesting times, or even exist on their periphery. &quot;Interesting&quot; in general just doesn't happen to them, neither by their own actions nor by those of others or the world at large.<br /> <br /> If I understand correctly, Lian is saying that yes, someone's effectively spirited away to the Hedge, but since Banality is so incredibly antithetical to story, the time for that to be relevant in any way, shape, or form is before a Sidhe is lost to it, not after.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I agree with it? But I can see the point: Banality is so uninteresting that its final cruelty here is that it doesn't even let your ending have dramatic tension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T08:36:23-08:00","id":1351048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body?p=1350852#post1350852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, maybe it's because I don't get the references, except for the CtL one, but I'm not totally sure what you're getting at here. Could you please clarify?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That someone had their body snatched is without a doubt True. If you want to engage in that plot as a thing. The Tithed were a concept brought up in End Times Book, and were recycled for the theoretical c5 musings. In a metaphysical truth, there is a person who's soul was carried off to Arcadia and very much might be having a &quot;Lost&quot; experience. Even in the Dreaming game. Or they might be Keremet Denizens.. you have some options to play up on the &quot;Fuck you body thief&quot;. There's all sorts of plots one can hang off of it.<br /> <br /> That Arcadian Sidhe are any different in Undoing isn't one of them and heavily undercuts the power of Banality. Dreams don't matter. Souls don't matter. I mean think of the undone almost as a Pzombie. It moves.. it shows everything that a person is supposed to do. But there's no inner light, no inner reflection. Its not something as interesting as a Coma patient though. Its frightening in that how much its able to keep moving without that light. How little the light of that person actually matters either as a Fairy or a Human.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T08:44:57-08:00","id":1351050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body?p=1351016#post1351016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I agree with it? But I can see the point: Banality is so uninteresting that its final cruelty here is that it doesn't even let your ending have dramatic tension.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not uninteresting. Banality is meant to be so frightening to the Fairies that they'd rather die. That they would kill for glamour. The Undone arcadian who slips into a coma and dies that would be a happish ending for them. There's closure. But that same friend walking around completely forgotten, completely blind to who they were. That's what frightens and drives them to act.<br /> <br /> I Mean imagine tomorrow a person you loved for decades... woke up and forgot you? They have a perfectly normal life, painfully normally really as it no longer includes you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T12:52:24-08:00","id":1351098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body?p=1351050#post1351050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not uninteresting. Banality is meant to be so frightening to the Fairies that they'd rather die. That they would kill for glamour. The Undone arcadian who slips into a coma and dies that would be a happish ending for them. There's closure. But that same friend walking around completely forgotten, completely blind to who they were. That's what frightens and drives them to act.<br /> <br /> I Mean imagine tomorrow a person you loved for decades... woke up and forgot you? They have a perfectly normal life, painfully normally really as it no longer includes you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A person that I loved very much was afflicted with Alzheimers disease. Parts of her just disappeared. To the extent that she became a different person entirely. But I came to love that lady too. When she passed, you could say that I cried for two dear ladies.<br /> <br /> So it makes me wonder; if a person who carried a fae soul, lost that soul, and if the bodies original soul returned, might it be an innocent? The soul of a child, returned to a body now grown cold from banality, and bowed with the weight of years, is a horrible thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T14:33:12-08:00","id":1351127,"title":"","content":"Alright I do think I get what you're saying now Lian and I can certainly see the thematic value in it although I might not always go with that myself for stories or chronicles, but I believe that I now understand what you were getting at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T15:41:31-08:00","id":1351143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body?p=1351098#post1351098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A person that I loved very much was afflicted with Alzheimers disease. Parts of her just disappeared. To the extent that she became a different person entirely. But I came to love that lady too. When she passed, you could say that I cried for two dear ladies..</div> </div> </div> </div>Having had a similar experience.. but one that turned out not as kindly. My Grandmother, went into full dementia in the last 10 years of her life. Everything she used to be was gone, but she could still &quot;function&quot; she was just this horrible bitter being that could even sense that she had lost so much but couldn't put her finger on it.<br /> <br /> So that's what I imagine being Undone is like... honestly I think she would have been happier without those ten years of misery.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349873-what-happens-to-an-undone-arcadian-sidhe-s-body?p=1351127#post1351127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright I do think I get what you're saying now Lian and I can certainly see the thematic value in it although I might not always go with that myself for stories or chronicles, but I believe that I now understand what you were getting at.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are definately other directions to take it in, I just think the stated base is that Arcadian SIdhe aren't special. That doesn't mean they can't be made that way. I know I'd make them MUCH more similar if I was playing a Crossover with Fallen so it looks like there's a distinct spectrum from Arcadian, to Hsien(who can be haunted by theirown ghosts!) to Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}